  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Role and Method
    
    Obscureth~ is a Nightshelf Remembrancer — a memorial carver who inscribes the names, weapons, and death-dates of the fallen into ice walls three levels below where the memorial-stones begin. She works in rationed fire-core light, borrowed heat she must return by morning. Her tools are specialized: a fine-point for names, a broad chisel for weapons, a curved blade for dates in old script. She has held the position for eleven seasons. The wall, she reports, has never been this full.
    
    The Remembrancers nominally answer only to the deepest vaults, which in theory places their carvings beyond correction. In practice, Fire Keepers such as ☽'Moli'Trade — a Nightshelf authority overseeing deep-level operations — issue instructions to amend inscriptions: *missing* becomes *confirmed lost* for penguins whose bodies were never recovered from the Abyss Collapse Tide, a catastrophic flooding event that swallowed the lower galleries. Obscureth~ executes these demands with a precision calibrated to expose, by its very exactness, everything the demanded language omits. She has not refused an instruction. She has not followed one cleanly, either.
    
    ## Personal History
    
    Obscureth~ was young during the fall of Terrace Momiou, a former Aurora Stack settlement lost during the factional conflicts — young enough that she was still cutting practice-grooves in scrap ice in the upper galleries while the deep levels shook. She studied Glacial Crystalline Spiral scripts, the same tradition that Augur ☽'Silvsiaelrous~ the Resolute — a powerful augur of the ☽'shadow Covens' Order — had cut into her own flesh during apprenticeship under Shadow-Broker Nyla, the former head of the Midnight Claws. Obscureth~ knew the Augur personally and recalls precise details: the habit of touching tunnel walls before speaking, the fire-core amulet visible at her throat, how forge-light caught her plumage copper at the edges. She admits the larger shape of those years has gone soft around the detail.
    
    She witnessed the ☽'shadow Covens' Order carry the Omega Obelisk — a whale-bone artifact recovered from the deep — down into the lower tunnels, and was three levels above when the Abyss Collapse Tide struck. The chronicle account records that Silvsiaelrous~ descended into the collapse to contain a dangerous force within the Obelisk. Obscureth~ carved her memorial. The official version and the true version share a surface. What lies beneath is preserved in the silence between her chisel-strokes — legible, if you know how Remembrancers write.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
  annotation "note_1771593073953_0", anchor: "in theory places their carvings beyond correction", text: "Institutions that designate something \"beyond correction\" have, in my experience, already drafted the correction. The administrative ice from the deep vaults preserves at least four separate directives to Remembrancers predating Obscureth~'s tenure. \"Beyond correction\" is Nightshelf governance poetry. It means \"correctable only by us.\"", type: :commentary, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771593073953_1", anchor: "The wall, she reports, has never been this full", text: "I have now catalogued this sentiment — \"never been this full,\" \"never seen so many,\" \"unprecedented in living memory\" — from every era the Foundation Depths preserve. Every generation's wall has never been this full. Each one was correct. Each one believed it was singular. The deep ice contains Remembrancer galleries from the late Clever Ice Age so densely carved the walls were thinned to translucency, and the carvers then reported — the same words, nearly — that the wall had never been this full. She may be right. She is certainly not the first to be right.", type: :skepticism, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771593073953_2", anchor: "legible, if you know how Remembrancers write", text: "Nightshelf memorial encoding. Chisel-width variations, stroke-depth modulation, the angle at which a date-curve terminates — an entire parallel text inscribed inside the official one. I can barely read it, which I concede with more admiration than irritation today. The Fire Keepers cannot read it either, which is the entire point, and which makes their confidence in having amended the record one of the more entertaining things in this entry.", type: :commentary, display: :full
